# Decimal literal scale preservation

Verifies decimal literals keep their source scale and accept exponent
notation through the complete CLI pipeline.

>>> source
scaled: decimal = 1.50
plain: decimal = 2.5
big: decimal = 1e3

// Verifies a trailing zero survives parsing and printing.
print(scaled)
print(plain)

// Verifies exponent notation denotes the same decimal value.
print(big)

<<< stdout
1.50
2.5
1000

<<< stderr
